# umi - the handheld collection pipeline.
#
# Print the marker solids, record the gripper cameras and the top camera, recover
# where the handheld gripper was against the desk dome. Nothing here touches the
# arms; this is the slice that collects demonstrations without the robot.

# OpenCV, for ArUco detection and solvePnP. Deliberately NOT
# opencv-contrib-python: aruco moved out of contrib and into the main objdetect
# module in OpenCV 4.7, so contrib buys nothing this needs - and installing it
# beside the opencv-python-headless that arrives with lerobot leaves two packages
# both owning `cv2`, whichever one wins being whichever was unpacked last.
opencv-python-headless>=4.7

# Solid geometry, for `pinkrab-umi marker`: the marker solids are cut as manifold
# booleans and written as STL. Only that command needs it - it is imported inside
# the function - but a slice that cannot run its own marker command is not whole.
manifold3d

# The other reader. OpenCV can decode the AprilTag families with its own ArUco
# pipeline, but that is the bit layout without the detector: on rendered frames
# of this solid the AprilTag library's own reader found 2.75 faces at 70 cm with
# a blurred hand against 1.50 the same family read by OpenCV, and its corners
# land two to five times closer. It is optional - settings.detector picks - so
# nothing here fails without it.
pupil-apriltags
pyobjc-framework-AVFoundation; sys_platform == "darwin"   # which USB socket each camera is in
